@hystudio/dsh-quota-pill README · What it reads：**DeepSeek works with no setup at all** if you are signed in to DeepSeek Platform
in DSH — that is the official account, and it is the one most users care about.

The three API-key providers need nothing but the key. The three OAuth providers
need CLIProxyAPI installed and logged in, because that is what holds the tokens;
this plugin only reads them and never runs an OAuth flow itself.

@hystudio/dsh-quota-pill README · Notes on specific providers：**Command Code** does not expose a monthly ceiling. The adapter derives it from
`monthlyCap = weekly.cap × 2`, an identity verified against two different plans
(31.6 + 38.4 = 70 with `weekly.cap` 35; 0.225 + 9.775 = 10 with `weekly.cap` 6).

@hystudio/dsh-quota-pill README · Notes on specific providers：Windows with a real reset period (5-hour / weekly / monthly) always render as a
percentage — including the 100% seen right after a reset — so a bucket never
switches units as it is spent. The credit counts stay in the row's tooltip;
only credit packs without a period render as credits.
